# Mail

This package owns the generated GoForj mail wiring.

Generated apps expose a mail manager through the application container and configure it from environment variables.

The generated mail manager imports only the drivers enabled by `MAIL_SUPPORTED_DRIVERS`. This keeps heavyweight driver dependencies, especially SES, out of the app unless they are explicitly enabled.

Named mailers use the same pattern as other GoForj primitives:

- MAIL_DRIVER configures the default mailer
- MAIL_<NAME>_DRIVER configures a named mailer
- MAIL_<NAME>_FROM_ADDRESS and MAIL_<NAME>_FROM_NAME override sender defaults for that named mailer

## Defaults

- `MAIL_DRIVER`
  - default: `log`
  - supported values: `log`, `smtp`, `resend`, `postmark`, `mailgun`, `sendgrid`, `ses`
- `MAIL_SUPPORTED_DRIVERS`
  - controls which mail drivers are generated into the app at compile time
  - if unset, generation falls back to the active `MAIL_DRIVER`
- `MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS`
  - required for real delivery
  - default generated value: `no-reply@example.com`
- `MAIL_FROM_NAME`
  - default generated value: `{{ .ProjectName }}`
- `MAIL_LOG_BODIES`
  - log-driver only
  - default: `false`

## Driver Settings

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Drivers | Expected Value | Default |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| MAIL_DRIVER | all | one driver name | log |
| MAIL_SUPPORTED_DRIVERS | all | comma-separated driver names | MAIL_DRIVER when unset |
| MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS | all | email address | no-reply@example.com |
| MAIL_FROM_NAME | all | display name | {{ .ProjectName }} |
| MAIL_LOG_BODIES | log | boolean | false |
| MAIL_SMTP_HOST | smtp | hostname | none |
| MAIL_SMTP_PORT | smtp | integer port | 587 |
| MAIL_SMTP_USERNAME | smtp | username | empty |
| MAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD | smtp | password | empty |
| MAIL_SMTP_IDENTITY | smtp | identity string | empty |
| MAIL_SMTP_FORCE_TLS | smtp | boolean | false |
| MAIL_RESEND_API_KEY | resend | API key | empty |
| MAIL_RESEND_ENDPOINT | resend | URL | provider default |
| MAIL_POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN | postmark | API token | empty |
| MAIL_POSTMARK_ENDPOINT | postmark | URL | provider default |
| MAIL_POSTMARK_MESSAGE_STREAM | postmark | stream name | empty |
| MAIL_MAILGUN_DOMAIN | mailgun | domain | empty |
| MAIL_MAILGUN_API_KEY | mailgun | API key | empty |
| MAIL_MAILGUN_ENDPOINT | mailgun | URL | provider default |
| MAIL_SENDGRID_API_KEY | sendgrid | API key | empty |
| MAIL_SENDGRID_ENDPOINT | sendgrid | URL | provider default |
| MAIL_SES_REGION | ses | AWS region | empty |
| MAIL_SES_ACCESS_KEY_ID | ses | AWS access key id | empty |
| MAIL_SES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY | ses | AWS secret access key | empty |
| MAIL_SES_SESSION_TOKEN | ses | AWS session token | empty |
| MAIL_SES_ENDPOINT | ses | URL | AWS SDK default |
| MAIL_SES_CONFIGURATION_SET | ses | configuration set name | empty |

### log

- writes mail delivery output to stdout
- useful for local development and smoke testing

### smtp

Gmail generally uses the SMTP driver with:

- host: `smtp.gmail.com`
- port: `587`
- app passwords instead of your normal account password

### resend

- API-based transactional delivery

### postmark

- API-based transactional delivery
- optional message stream support

### mailgun

- domain-based API delivery

### sendgrid

- API-based transactional delivery

### ses

- AWS-backed delivery
- heavier dependency surface than the other API drivers

## Usage

The generated app exposes the configured mail manager through `App.Mail()`.

Auth delivery uses this component automatically when both `Auth` and `Mail` are enabled.

## Named Mailers

The default mailer remains the default path for framework features like auth.

Named mailers are optional and can be used when an app wants more than one configured sender.

Named mailers are generated from MAIL_<NAME>_* environment variables during forj generate. In normal workflows this is usually picked up automatically through forj build, and therefore passively during forj dev on code changes. If you add a new named mailer, generation must run so the named accessor is emitted into the app source.

Example env:

MAIL_DRIVER=log
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=no-reply@example.com
MAIL_FROM_NAME={{ .ProjectName }}

MAIL_TRANSACTIONAL_DRIVER=resend
MAIL_TRANSACTIONAL_FROM_ADDRESS=transactions@example.com
MAIL_TRANSACTIONAL_FROM_NAME={{ .ProjectName }} Transactions
MAIL_TRANSACTIONAL_RESEND_API_KEY=...

Example usage:

manager := app.Mail()
defaultMailer := manager.Default()
transactional := manager.Transactional()
support := manager.Named("support")
